{
  "model": "E4419B",
  "manufacturer": "Agilent/Keysight",
  "title": "Agilent E4419B Power Meter",
  "manual": "E4418B Service.pdf: Keysight E4418B/E4419B Service Guide, Chapter 2 Performance Tests; cross-checked against E4418-90064.pdf (Agilent edition)",
  "busDriver": "E4419B",
  "defaultResource": "GPIB0::13::INSTR",
  "channels": [
    "A",
    "B"
  ],
  "warmupMinutes": 30,
  "notes": [
    "Over SCPI the app does each channel's steps as for the E4418B, on channel n (CAL<n>, SENS<n>, UNIT<n>), and reads READ<n>? DEF,DEF,(@<n>), n = 1 for A and 2 for B: the source list names the channel, so the window set-up does not matter (E4418B/E4419B Programming Guide, pp. 2-22 to 2-23).",
    "The Service Guide gives the E4418B key presses; on the E4419B the equivalent key presses are made on both channels (notes on pp. 2-6, 2-8 and 2-12), with the same limits (Tables 2-2 and 2-4 have Channel A and Channel B columns)."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "id": "zero-test",
      "title": "Zero Test",
      "perChannel": true,
      "source": "E4418B Service Guide, pp. 2-5 to 2-6 (PDF pp. 45-46), Table 2-2",
      "reading": "Meter",
      "equipment": [
        "HP 11683A Range Calibrator",
        "HP 11730A power sensor cable"
      ],
      "setup": [
        "Connect the 11683A to the channel under test with the 11730A (Figure 2-1 shows channel A). Press Local, Preset, Confirm; dBm/W, W.",
        "11683A: RANGE 3 µW, POLARITY NORMAL, FUNCTION STANDBY, LINE ON. Wait for the downward drift to stop (typically under 60 s).",
        "System, Inputs, Input Settings, More, Filter: On, Mode Man, Length 512, Enter.",
        "Zero/Cal, Zero; wait about 10 s, then 30 s more before reading."
      ],
      "meter": {
        "display": "Watts",
        "filter": 512
      },
      "zero": {
        "calibrator": {
          "range": "3uW",
          "function": "Standby",
          "polarity": "Normal"
        },
        "settleSeconds": 60
      },
      "points": [
        {
          "label": "Zero, filter 512",
          "calibrator": {
            "range": "3uW",
            "function": "Standby",
            "polarity": "Normal"
          },
          "meterSetting": "W, filter 512, after Zero (no Cal)",
          "expected": 0,
          "unit": "nW",
          "min": -76.4,
          "max": 76.4,
          "note": "Table 2-2 limits ±76.40 nW; step 8 text says ±0.05 µW."
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Spec: zero set ±0.0764 µW (range calibrator zero set ±0.05 µW plus noise at 512 averages)."
      ]
    },
